[38;2;124;124;124mThe problem asks: For an algebraic group $G$ and a number field $F/\mathbb{Q}$, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mdetermine if the Weil restriction of $G(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ from $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{Q}$ to $F$ is equal to $G(\mathbb{A}_{F})$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFirst, let me clarify the setup. We have an algebraic group $G$ (presumably [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdefined over $\mathbb{Q}$, or over $F$). The question is about Weil restriction.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mWeil restriction (restriction of scalars) $\operatorname{Res}_{F/\mathbb{Q}}$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtakes an algebraic group (or variety) defined over $F$ and produces one defined [0m[38;2;124;124;124mover $\mathbb{Q}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about what the question is really asking.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me re-read: "the Weil restriction of $G(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ [0m[38;2;124;124;124mfrom $\mathbb{Q}$ to $F$"[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mHmm, this is a bit ambiguous. Let me think about the standard relationship.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe key fact is: if $G$ is an algebraic group over $\mathbb{Q}$, then there's a [0m[38;2;124;124;124mnatural isomorphism[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\operatorname{Res}_{F/\mathbb{Q}}(G \times_{\mathbb{Q}} F)(\mathbb{A}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m_{\mathbb{Q}}) \cong G(\mathbb{A}_F)$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is the fundamental property of Weil restriction and adelic points.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mMore precisely, for $H = \operatorname{Res}_{F/\mathbb{Q}}(G_F)$ where $G_F = G [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\times_{\mathbb{Q}} F$, we have:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$H(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}) = \operatorname{Res}_{F/\mathbb{Q}}(G_F)(\mathbb{A}[0m[38;2;124;124;124m_{\mathbb{Q}}) \cong G(\mathbb{A}_F)$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a standard and fundamental result.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, the question asks whether "the Weil restriction of $G(\mathbb{A}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m_{\mathbb{Q}})$ from $\mathbb{Q}$ to $F$" equals $G(\mathbb{A}_F)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mI think the question is asking about the relationship between $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\operatorname{Res}_{F/\mathbb{Q}}(G)(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ and $G(\mathbb{A}[0m[38;2;124;124;124m_F)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe answer is YES, they are equal (naturally isomorphic).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me prove this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Setup:** Let $G$ be an algebraic group over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $F/\mathbb{Q}$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mbe a number field (finite extension). Let $G_F = G [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}} \operatorname{Spec} F$ be the base change[0m[38;2;124;124;124mof $G$ to $F$. The Weil restriction $\operatorname{Res}_{F/\mathbb{Q}}(G_F)$ is [0m[38;2;124;124;124man algebraic group over $\mathbb{Q}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Claim:** $\operatorname{Res}_{F/\mathbb{Q}}(G_F)(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\cong G(\mathbb{A}_F)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Proof:**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe defining property of Weil restriction is that for any $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$R$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\operatorname{Res}_{F/\mathbb{Q}}(G_F)(R) = G_F(R \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} F) = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mG(R \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} F)$$[0m

